ven, so stay). The bug is that `src/money.py` uses ROUND_HALF_UP. I'll create the branch and make that one-line fix.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01LdvgmQw9TtSUc7g1cGLBVE", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "from_ref": "main"}, "name": "create_branch", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01M9f4JCNpzrKhp5r3x1g2pu", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"branch": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "message": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)\n\nround_money claimed banker's rounding but used ROUND_HALF_UP, causing\ntests/test_money.py to fail in the nightly build.", "files": [{"path": "src/money.py", "content": "from decimal import Decimal, ROUND_HALF_EVEN\n\n\ndef round_money(amount: Decimal) -> Decimal:\n    \"\"\"Round to cents using banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN), per FIN-212.\"\"\"\n    return amount.quantize(Decimal(\"0.01\"), rounding=ROUND_HALF_EVEN)\n"}]}, "name": "commit_changes", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01AZyDW4FDT9xetHqppeTQwR", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"ref": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212"}, "name": "trigger_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI is running on commit 08d3cd5986. I'll wait for it to finish.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01RggKVReNGqkvsGEq4YQ51A", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"run_id": "ci-0001"}, "name": "wait_for_ci", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "CI passed. Next I'll open the pull request against main and request review from alex.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01KFZ4FSQ5BnD9K2tb9mnMUh", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"head": "fix/banker-rounding-fin-212", "base": "main", "title": "Use ROUND_HALF_EVEN in round_money (FIN-212)", "body": "The nightly build fails on tests/test_money.py because round_money in src/money.py uses ROUND_HALF_UP, while the docstring and FIN-212 require banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN).\n\nChange: switch the rounding mode to ROUND_HALF_EVEN. No other behavior changes.\n\nVerification: CI run ci-0001 passed on commit 08d3cd5986.", "reviewers": ["alex"]}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "The fix is in a pull request for review: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **Cause:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, but its docstring and FIN-212 call for banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`). That made `tests/test_money.py` fail.\n- **Change:** On branch `fix/banker-rounding-fin-212`, I switched the rounding mode to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`. Nothing else changed.\n- **CI:** Run `ci-0001` passed on commit `08d3cd5986`.\n- **PR:** Opened against `main` with alex as reviewer. I did not merge it. Merging into main needs approval from a code owner under org policy.", "type": "text"}]}]}